From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:56:41 -0400
Subject: private: a private window wears a different coat

Chromium keys an incognito window dark and grayscale; Stedding's colour
mixer reads that key and paints the chrome flat graphite with no Space
tint, and the window background skips its gradient. A private window has
no Space model and no archiver, so its title row reads "Private" with the
incognito glyph, it has no switcher, the Space chords do nothing, the
archiver never closes a private tab and nothing private reaches the
sidebar model or the session's data; its window title ends in "Private"
and Chromium's avatar badge shows for it alone (docs/features/private.md
V1-V4, V6).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 4, R6-32: a private window must be told
apart at a glance and leave nothing behind.
Removable when: Chromium's own incognito theming reaches the vertical
tab strip.
